\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar flat but seen staying in precarious state.  \b0\par\par\uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 2003\par 03:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Dec 29 (Reuters) - The dollar moved sideways in holiday-thinned trade on Monday, with traders waiting to see if its persistent decline over the past year will resume when many players return to the market after Christmas holidays.  \par \par \uc2 Structural problems that have pushed down the dollar for much of this year - such as worries over extremists' attacks on the United States and the yawning U.S. current account deficit - are likely to keep nagging at it, they said.  \par \par \uc2 "I think the dollar will be capped this week," said Shogo Nagaya, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Nomura Trust and Banking.  \par \par \uc2 "Geopolitical risk remains. And there's no change in the fact that capital inflows to the U.S. are dwindling."  \par \par \uc2 But others argued that any further decline in the dollar could be limited.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't think EU finance ministers are very pleased about the euro's recent strength," said Toru Umemoto, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Morgan Stanley in Tokyo, adding that they could voice such concerns at a meeting of Group of Seven (G7) nations' finance ministers due early in the new year.  \par \par \uc2 As of 0152 GMT, the euro was at $1.2434/39 flat from late U.S. trade and not far from its record high around $1.2470 hit last week. It was also flat around 133.45 yen  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was slightly easier at 107.17/25 yen, versus 107.45 yen in late Friday U.S. trade.  \par \par \uc2 Traders suspect the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday when the dollar hit a two-week low of 106.93 yen, approaching its three-year trough of 106.74 hit earlier this month.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said on Friday that Japan would act on exchange rates if the market strayed from economic fundamentals.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said on Friday that the Bank of Japan had agreed to a government request for short-term funding to soothe worries it may soon run out of funds to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 The BOJ policy board agreed to issue three-month repo pacts for up to 10 trillion yen ($93 billion).  \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will almost certainly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  so I don't think many players will want to push dollar/yen down," said Morgan Stanley's Umemoto. ($1=107.26 Yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031229dzct000ji\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
