\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Japan \highlight\uc2  Dec  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Data Tuesday  \b0\par\par\uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 2003\par 08:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 With the euro apparently gearing up to test new highs against the dollar, market participants wondered at what point European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policymakers would express concern about the impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength. The dollar has fallen about 13% against the euro since September.  \par \par \uc2 A report in Monday's Financial Times said ECB officials are "becoming increasingly uneasy about the euro's rise, fearing it could move substantially higher and undermine the fragile eurozone recovery."  \par \par \uc2 The long-looming risks of global economic imbalances and U.S.' twin budget and current account deficits "are now materializing," the report quoted an unnamed senior official as saying.  \par \par \uc2 "We are clearly not surprised by what is happening... but the decline of the dollar has been relatively sharp," the official added.  \par \par \uc2 Some Asian market participants said the key reasons for the dollar's drop were based in the U.S., not in Europe.  \par \par \uc2 "It's not the euro that's too strong, it's the dollar that's weak. The problem lies with the dollar, and the U.S.' twin deficits," said Ryohei Muramatsu, Commerzbank manager of Group Treasury Asia.  \par \par \uc2 Looking ahead, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will release December \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  figures On Tuesday at 0900 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 Tokyo traders said the amount could be as high as Y2 trillion-Y3 trillion, as some believe the Bank of Japan sold as much as Y1 trillion to push the yen off its high of Y106.74 hit against the dollar on Dec. 9.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent Y17.8 trillion in yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first eleven months of the year.  \par \par \uc2 -By Lisa Twaronite, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; lisa.twaronite@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by John Gibson and Bennett Richardson  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \par \par \uc2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031229dzct00057\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
