\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar hovers as geopolitical worries nag.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By John Parry  \par \uc2 691 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Dezember 2003\par 18:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Dec 26 (Reuters) - The dollar hovered in narrow ranges on Friday in holiday-thinned trading while market sentiment remained bearish amid concerns that Al Qaeda may try to launch attacks against the United States.  \par \par \uc2 A lack of momentum in scant post-Christmas trade and wariness about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities prevented the dollar from plunging to new lows against the euro and from retesting three-year lows set against the yen earlier this month.  \par \par \uc2 "We still have concerns over acts of terrorism after the cancellation of Air France flights to the United States. That of course remains at the fore," said Andrew Delano, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at IDEAglobal in New York.  \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Air France canceled Christmas flights from Paris to Los Angeles after U.S. intelligence found the name of at least one person suspected of having links to extremist groups on the passenger list. U.S. officials relayed "credible, reliable" intelligence reports to France regarding plans for "near-term simultaneous attacks that would rival Sept. 11," a U.S. official said.  \par \par \uc2 Air France said on Friday it will resume its Paris-Los Angeles flights after French intelligence found nothing to substantiate U.S. suspicions about the one passenger having links to terror groups.  \par \par \uc2 "The geopolitical situation is rearing its head again and has become more of a concern...That is just not going to help the dollar," said Tim Mazanec, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Investors Bank & Trust in Boston.  \par \par \uc2 In early afternoon New York trading, the euro hovered not far below record highs of $1.2470 against the dollar, trading at $1.2435, down 0.1 percent on the day but still within sight of the psychologically important $1.2500 mark.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the dollar was down 0.07 percent to 107.14 yen , while traders became wary about possible Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen, given the market's low liquidity in post-Christmas trading.  \par \par \uc2 "The market worry is that the Bank of Japan might come in if we get a (dollar) move below 107 yen," said Mazanec.  \par \par \uc2 Against the Swiss franc, the dollar was trading at 1.2520 francs , up 0.3 percent on the day. The pound, meanwhile, was up 0.06 percent at $1.7726 . U.K. markets are shut until Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Virtually all traders in London and New York were off for Christmas on Thursday and many in New York were likely to take Friday off as well, keeping global volume subdued.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  WORRIES  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the market appeared hesitant to push the dollar below 107 yen for fear it could prompt Japanese authorities, who have been worried that a stronger yen could stall \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export-led economic recovery, to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and send the dollar sharply back up.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki, repeating his warning against the yen's recent gains against the dollar, told a news conference that Japan would act on exchange rates if the market strayed from economic fundamentals.  \par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said the Bank of Japan has agreed to a government request for short-term funding to soothe worries it may soon run out of funds to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The BoJ policy board agreed to issue three-month repo pacts for up to 10 trillion yen, but noted that this was a temporary, precautionary measure.  \par \par \uc2 Most analysts were convinced that the dollar is due for a near-term rally fairly soon, given the extent of its losses in the past few sessions. "The market is heavily extended in short dollar positions, so the dollar is due for a pullback. But I'm not sure what (the) catalyst would be," said IDEAglobal's Delano.  \par \par \uc2 Among U.S. economic data that might move the dollar next week is the widely watched Institute for Supply Management nationwide report on manufacturing. But judging by the dollar's recent tendency to shrug at economic data, it might take a clear upside surprise to offer the beleaguered greenback more than fleeting relief.  \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Gertrude Chavez in New York and Shinichi Kishima in Tokyo).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031227dzcq002pd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
