\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Japan MOF taps BOJ to beef up  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  war chest.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Satomi Noguchi  \par \uc2 579 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Dezember 2003\par 09:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Dec 26 (Reuters) - Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF), in a bid to quell speculation that it could run out of cash to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, said on Friday it could now raise funds by selling foreign bonds to the Bank of Japan.  \par \par \uc2 Confirming a scheme which government officials had unveiled to Reuters earlier in the day, the ministry said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could provide up to 10 trillion yen ($93.2 billion) for its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account by buying foreign bonds - namely U.S. Treasuries - from it under repurchase agreements.  \par \par \uc2 The move comes within a week of the ministry's announcement that it would raise the legal ceiling for its issuance of short-term bills for its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  account, a measure aimed at removing any speculation about a possible funding crunch.  \par \par \uc2 Such speculation in itself had exacerbated the yen's rise to three-year highs against the dollar earlier this month, prompting the authorities to emphasize the abundance of funds available to them to beat back the buoyant \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and prevent Japan's export-led economic recovery from stalling.  \par \par \uc2 A MOF official insisted the authorities still had ample funds and the latest deal with the BOJ was a precautionary measure.  \par \par \uc2 "There is still room for us," a ministry official told reporters. "It doesn't mean we'll immediately use it."  \par \par \uc2 "It is quite possible that there may be no actual selling (of foreign bonds)," he added.  \par \par \uc2 The BOJ, which held a board meeting earlier on Friday to approve the plan, said in a statement that it would provide yen funds as a temporary measure when the MOF felt it necessary.  \par \par \uc2 MORE AMMUNITION  \par \par \uc2 The increase in the MOF's borrowing limit, spelled out in the draft budget for fiscal 2004/05, would not be formally legislated until late January and the deal with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen as a stop-gap measure.  \par \par \uc2 "It's a very technical issue. That they have a bigger borrowing limit now doesn't necessarily mean they will be more aggressive in their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Junya Tanase, global markets officer at JP Morgan Chase in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 "But it does allow them to continue the current policy, which we think is aimed at smoothing the dollar's decline."  \par \par \uc2 Last Saturday, the ministry drafted a supplementary budget for the fiscal year ending in March in which the borrowing ceiling for its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  account, via issuance of so-called finance bills (FBs), was raised to 100 trillion yen from 79 trillion yen.  \par \par \uc2 The FB ceiling was further jacked up to 140 trillion yen in the draft budget for fiscal 2004/05, also unveiled on Saturday.  \par \par \uc2 Because it would take until at least late January for the extra budget to be legislated, the BOJ repo would provide a cushion should the MOF see the need to step up its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has conducted a record 17.8 trillion yen of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first 11 months of this year, raising concerns that it was nearing the borrowing limit.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar, which has fallen more than 10 percent from early August heights above 120 yen, hit three-year lows below 107 yen earlier this month, fuelling worries that a recovery in Japan's export-reliant economy could be choked off.  \par \par \uc2 On Friday, the dollar was drifting just above 107 yen in thin post-Christmas trade. ($1=107.28 Yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031226dzcq0025y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
