\par\par \b \uc2 Japan MOF asks BOJ to help beef up  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  war chest.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Satomi Noguchi  \par \uc2 463 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Dezember 2003\par 06:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Dec 26 (Reuters) - Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF), in a bid to quell speculation that it could soon run out of funds to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, has asked the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) for short-term funding, a government source said on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The MOF, whose holding of U.S. Treasury securities has bulged with the hundreds of billions of dollars it has bought for yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the years, has asked the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy foreign bonds under a repurchase agreement to provide short-term funds in yen, the source said.  \par \par \uc2 The BOJ policy board met on Friday to discuss the issue and agreed to three-month repo pacts, for up to a total of 10 trillion yen ($93.2 billion), the source said.  \par \par \uc2 A BOJ official declined to comment on the issue.  \par \par \uc2 The move comes within a week of another move by the MOF to replenish its war chest for yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , aimed at preventing a higher yen from derailing \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export-led economic recovery.  \par \par \uc2 Last Saturday, the ministry drafted a supplementary budget for the fiscal year ending in March in which the borrowing ceiling for its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  account was jacked up to 100 trillion yen from 79 trillion yen.  \par \par \uc2 The ceiling was further raised to 140 trillion yen in the draft budget for fiscal 2004/05, also unveiled on Saturday.  \par \par \uc2 Because it would take until at least late January for the extra budget to be legislated, the repo pact with the BOJ would provide a cushion should the MOF see the need to step up its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 RECORD \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has conducted a record 17.8 trillion yen of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first 11 months of this year, raising concerns that it was nearing the limit for its issuance of short-term finance bills (FBs) - the main funding tool for the MOF's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  account.  \par \par \uc2 MOF officials have sought to play down such worries, insisting they still had ample funding room under the cap but that they had raised the ceiling so as to retain the ability to respond flexibly in the event of an unforeseen development in the market. Earlier on Friday, Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki reiterated that Japan would take appropriate action on exchange rates if the market strayed from economic fundamentals.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar, which has fallen more than 10 percent from early August heights above 120 yen, hit three-year lows below 107 yen earlier this month, fuelling worries that a recovery in Japan's export-reliant economy could be choked off.  \par \par \uc2 On Friday, the dollar was drifting around 107.10 yen in thin post-Christmas trade. ($1=107.28 Yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031226dzcq001gx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
