\par\par \b \uc2 WRAP: BOJ To Have Funds Ready To Help MOF's  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Action  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Leika Kihara & Miyako Takebe  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 645 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Dezember 2003\par 10:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will provide funds to the government for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if needed, as Tokyo continues its aggressive campaign to keep down the yen, the Bank of Japan and Finance Ministry said Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The BOJ will be ready to lend up to Y10 trillion in funds by buying U.S. Treasury bonds from the ministry on repurchase agreements, the two said.  \par \par \uc2 The temporary deal comes as repeated heavy yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year has caused Tokyo to get close to its legal limit for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , forcing it wait to for an increase in that spending limit to be approved by parliament.  \par \par \uc2 The ministry's funding limit for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is slated to rise by Y21 trillion to Y100 trillion this fiscal year ending March, and then is set to be lifted to Y140 trillion next fiscal year, but those increases need to be approved by parliament, which won't convene until early next year.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has officially spent Y17.8 trillion in yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first eleven months of the year, bringing the cumulative \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  total to about Y72 trillion.  \par \par \uc2 But some market participants think the ministry might have sold Y2 trillion more since the end of the month, meaning it only has about Y5 trillion left in its Y79 trillion war chest for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 With the BOJ's agreement to supply \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds, however, the ministry won't have to worry about the yen's surging on speculation that it is running out of funds in the run-up to parliamentary approval for rises in the funding limit.  \par \par \uc2 "MOF's making sure that its arsenal is fully stocked, especially as it may need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily over the year-end (and) New Year's holidays when speculators might use thin liquidity to push the dollar lower toward Y105 - a level MOF is likely keen to defend," said Minoru Shioiri, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Mitsubishi Securities.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    BOJ Wants To Help MOF's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Action \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite the heavy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the yen on Friday was around Y107.00 to the dollar compared with about Y119.90 at the end of last year, as traders have become worried that the U.S.'s huge trade and budget deficits might drag down the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , while they have become more bullish toward Japan.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BOJ said the repo deals will be conducted if the Finance Ministry decides it doesn't have enough funds in the government's special \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  account, which sets aside money for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Considering current economic and financial conditions, the BOJ said it thought it ought to provide funds the government needs "to continue to respond flexibly to moves in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it will stop buying Treasury bonds from the ministry at the end of March next year, and the repo agreements will expire within three months of the transactions being conducted, except if the date of the repurchase is set before March 31.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In that case, the repurchase period can be extended by three months from the day after the initial repurchase date, until the government gets the funds needed to buy back the bonds, the BOJ said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A Finance Ministry official told reporters that the ministry will decide how much Treasurys to sell to the BOJ based on conditions in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The official said the ministry and BOJ decided on the Y10-trillion figure because Tokyo has spent around Y5 trillion in a single month on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the past, and double that seemed a comfortable amount.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Leika Kihara and Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com, leika.kihara@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Bennett Richardson  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031226dzcq0005i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
