\par\par \b \uc2 BOJ/MOF To Ensure MOF Has Enough  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Funds  \b0\par\par\uc2 467 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Dezember 2003\par 08:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Friday it will provide the Finance Ministry with up to Y10 trillion in funds by buying U.S. Treasury bonds from the ministry on repurchase agreements if requested.  \par \par \uc2 The temporary deal, which will expire at the end of March next year, is aimed at ensuring the Finance Ministry has enough funds to conduct \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the repo deals will be conducted if the Finance Ministry decides it doesn't have enough funds in the government's special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account, which sets aside money for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 It said it decided that considering current economic and financial conditions, the BOJ ought to provide funds the government needs "to continue to respond flexibly to moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market."  \par \par \uc2 The BOJ's provision of funds to the ministry is a stopgap measure so that the ministry, which has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the yen from rising, has enough ammunition to continue with the market action.  \par \par \uc2 The ministry's funding limit for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is slated to rise by Y21 trillion to Y100 trillion this fiscal year ending March, and then is set to increase to Y140 trillion next fiscal year, but those increases need to be approved by parliament.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has officially spent Y17.8 trillion in yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first eleven months of the year, bringing the cumulative \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  total to about Y72 trillion.  \par \par \uc2 But some market participants think the ministry might have sold Y2 trillion more since the end of the month, meaning it only has about Y5 trillion left in its Y79 trillion war chest for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Despite the heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yen on Friday was around Y107.00 compared with about Y119.90 at the end of last year, as market players have become worried that the U.S.'s huge trade and budget deficits might drag down the dollar, while they have become more bullish toward Japan.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan said it will stop buying Treasury bonds from the ministry at the end of March next year, and the repo agreements will expire within three months of the transactions being conducted, except if the date of the repurchase is set before March 31.  \par \par \uc2 In that case, the repurchase period can be extended by three months until the government gets the funds needed to buy back the bonds, the BOJ said.  \par \par \uc2 A Finance Ministry official told reporters that the ministry will decide how much Treasurys to sell to the BOJ based on conditions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 -By Kenneth McCallum and Leika Kihara, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; ken.mccallum@dowjones.com, leika.kihara@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Bennett Richardson  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031226dzcq00041\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgo