\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Options: Volatalities Firm After Dollar's New Lows  \b0\par\par\uc2 617 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 2003\par 19:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Volatilities implied by one-month euro/dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options edged up in New York Monday after the euro hit another all-time high in overnight trading.  \par \par \uc2 In part spooked by the U.S. government raising the U.S. terror threat level over the weekend by one notch to its second-highest level possible, dealers in London sold the dollar down to another record low against the euro.  \par \par \uc2 This gave volatilities a bid tone. But activity is winding down ahead of the Christmas holiday this week, liquidity is thin and few dealers are willing to add to existing positions.  \par \par \uc2 As a result, volatilities, like spot rates, remain within ranges. The euro's subsequent decline from that $1.2447 high to around $1.24 also helped cap volatilities.  \par \par \uc2 "Traders had thought a very slow climb in euro/dollar would limit vol rises and even initiate a drop, but the market is nervous with the increased terror alert in the U.S.," said Thomas Rogers, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at IFR \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Watch. "The outlook for higher vols should therefore be limited and traders are expecting spot prices to remain stable this week."  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said options trade was light, although slightly more concentrated around short-dated expiries between now and the end of the year.  \par \par \uc2 "But apart from that, most people have got positions on because they want them on," said a dealer at a large U.S. bank in New York, adding that he sees little change in spot rates or volatilities for the rest of the week.  \par \par \uc2 Around 1:30 p.m. EST Monday, in the over-the-counter market, one-month at-the-money (ATM) euro/dollar options implied volatility of 10.00%/10.40%, slightly up from 9.85%/10.05% in Tokyo earlier Monday and 9.80%/10.10% in New York Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Volatilities implied by one-month dollar/yen options were slightly higher at 8.10%/8.40% from 7.95%/8.20% in Tokyo Monday and 8.00%/8.30% in New York Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's persistent weakness against the yen is keeping the market on high alert for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Japanese monetary authorities.  \par \par \uc2 As reported, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it will put another Y61 million in its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  war chest. Although the news indicates that the Bank of Japan might be more aggressive in the future, it also suggests that the authorities might be preparing for an even greater battle in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets next year than it had this year. So far this year, Japan has sold nearly Y18 trillion in trying to prevent the yen from appreciating too much.  \par \par \uc2 "They (MOF) saw the future and they saw more dollar weakness," said a dealer at a U.K. bank in New York.  \par \par \uc2 Around 1:30 p.m. EST Monday, one-month at-the-money ATM dollar/yen options implied volatility of 8.10%/8.40%, up from 7.95%/8.20% in Tokyo Monday and 8.00%/8.30% in New York Friday.  \par \par \uc2 One-month ATM euro/yen options implied volatility of 8.00%/8.30%, compared with 7.95%/8.20% and 7.90%/8.05%.  \par \par \uc2 One-month quarter delta risk-reversals favored euro call/dollar put options by 0.3%/0.7%, and dollar put/yen call options by 0.4%/0.8%.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was trading at $1.2420, up from $1.2375 Friday in New York and unchanged against the yen at Y133.40. The dollar was trading at Y107.42, down from Y107.80.  \par \par \uc2 -By Jamie McGeever, Dow Jones Newswires; 201 938 2096; jamie.mcgeever@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 1077 4127 44427  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031222dzcm000ps\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
