\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar at life lows vs euro again, ECB in focus.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Justyna Pawlak  \par \uc2 689 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2003\par 14:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Dec 18 (Reuters) - The dollar hit record lows against the euro for a fifth straight session on Thursday on a growing view that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not try for now to influence the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's course.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been under heavy pressure on investor concern about the country's widening current account deficit and expectations that U.S. interest rates will remain steady for some time.  \par \par \uc2 A series of comments from euro zone officials also drove markets to believe the resulting strength of the euro was not likely to prompt \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.  \par \par \uc2 An upbeat Ifo business survey also suggested German firms were taking the euro's gains in their stride. "The degree of the euro's appreciation has been fairly orderly and we are seeing comments from ECB officials...who are not overly concerned about current levels so the euro continues to appreciate," said Trevor Dinsmore, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank in London.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell as low as $1.2436 per euro, according to Reuters data, beating the previous session's record low of $1.2422. But it had retreated to below $1.23 by 1300 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 The euro has gained more than 18 percent in value against the dollar so far this year, and about 50 percent since it hit record lows in 2000.  \par \par \uc2 The euro zone's central bankers were due to meet on Thursday but were not scheduled to make decisions on interest rates. Any announcements on other issues would be made at 1330 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. weekly jobless claims, also due at 1330 GMT, were expected to show a total of 365,000 new filings.  \par \par \uc2 The Philadelphia Federal Reserve Bank was due to release its December business activity survey at 1700 GMT. The index was seen down slightly to 25.4 from 25.9 in November.  \par \par \uc2 ECB SEEN KEEPING COOL  \par \par \uc2 German data showed business confidence rising for an eighth month running in December in the euro zone's largest economy.  \par \par \uc2 The Ifo economic research institute said its west German business climate index rose more than expected to 96.8, its highest level since the start of 2001 and up from 95.7 in November.  \par \par \uc2 However, the euro zone's economic performance was overshadowed by speculation that comments from ECB officials signalled little readiness to step into the market to stop the euro just yet.  \par \par \uc2 "The euro/dollar rate has not been driven by economic fundamentals. The Ifo increase was all frontloaded into expectations as opposed to current conditions, but this was not the focus of the market," said Kamal Sharma, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Wasserstein in London.  \par \par \uc2 ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet and governing council member Nout Wellink both repeated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's standard line that a strong and stable euro is in the interest of the euro zone's economy.  \par \par \uc2 ECB sources were also reported on Wednesday as saying the ECB was unlikely to consider \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the euro reaches $1.35.  \par \par \uc2 Ifo president Hans Werner Sinn also said the effect of the euro's rise on German businesses was "ambiguous".  \par \par \uc2 "They (ECB) don't want to be seen as considering \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Niels Christensen, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Societe Generale in Paris. "They don't want to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at these levels because it's not a strong euro story, it's a weak dollar story."  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the dollar was around 107.50 yen, little changed on the day. Sterling remained firm, holding at around $1.7650, but below Wednesday's 11-year high near $1.7700.  \par \par \uc2 Investors were on watch for any signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with speculation intensifying the government is set to announce a higher borrowing limit for funds for its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Government sources have told Reuters Japan would raise the cap on its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account to 100 trillion yen ($931.2 billion) for the fiscal year ending next March from the current ceiling of 79 trillion yen, giving \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  more scope to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the yen.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031218dzci0032d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
