\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar at yet another low vs euro, ECB stance eyed.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Justyna Pawlak  \par \uc2 670 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2003\par 11:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Dec 18 (Reuters) - The dollar hit record lows against the euro for a fifth straight session on Thursday on a growing view that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would let the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  run free at current levels.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been under heavy pressure for a while on investor concern about the country's widening current account deficit and expectations that U.S. interest rates will remain steady for some time.  \par \par \uc2 A series of comments from euro zone officials also drove markets to believe the resulting strength of the euro was not likely to prompt \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.  \par \par \uc2 "They don't want to be seen as considering \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Niels Christensen, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Societe Generale in Paris.  \par \par \uc2 "They don't want to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at these levels because it's not a strong euro story, it's a weak dollar story. The ECB itself cannot change the direction of the dollar."  \par \par \uc2 By 1030 GMT the dollar fell as low as $1.2436 per euro, according to Reuters data, beating the previous session's record low of $1.2422.  \par \par \uc2 So far this year, the euro has gained more than 18 percent of its value against the dollar and about 50 percent since the it hit record lows in 2000.  \par \par \uc2 The euro zone's central bankers were due to meet on Thursday but were not scheduled to make decisions on interest rates. Any announcements on other issues would be made at 1330 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 ECB MEMBERS SPEAK OUT  \par \par \uc2 German data showed business confidence rising for an eighth month running in December in the euro zone's largest economy.  \par \par \uc2 The Ifo economic research institute said its business climate index rose more than expected to 96.8, its highest level since the start of 2001 and up from 95.7 in November.  \par \par \uc2 However, the euro zone's economic performance was overshadowed by speculation that comments from ECB officials signalled little readiness to step into the market to stop the euro just yet.  \par \par \uc2 ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet was quoted saying he was happy both Europe and the United States were aiming to keep their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strong and stable.  \par \par \uc2 His comments came a day after ECB chief economist Otmar Issing was quoted as saying the euro's exchange rate against the dollar was back to normal, having reached the same level as around the time of its introduction of $1.17 in 1999.  \par \par \uc2 ECB sources were also reported on Wednesday as saying the ECB was unlikely to consider \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the euro reaches $1.35.  \par \par \uc2 Ifo president Hans Werner Sinn also said the effect of the euro's rise on German businesses was "ambiguous".  \par \par \uc2 "The euro's move is orderly so far and euro zone policymakers are not worried about the euro and perhaps the opposite - they see higher inflation but they don't want to raise rates yet. A stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  eases inflation," said Benedikt Germanier, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS in Zurich.  \par \par \uc2 NEW RELEASES  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the dollar was around 107.50 yen, little changed on the day. Sterling remained firm, holding at around $1.7650, but below Wednesday's 11-year high near $1.7700.  \par \par \uc2 Investors were on watch for any signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with speculation intensifying the government is set to announce a higher borrowing limit for funds for its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Government sources have told Reuters Japan would raise the cap on its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account to 100 trillion yen ($931.2 billion) for the fiscal year ending next March from the current ceiling of 79 trillion yen, giving \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  more scope to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. weekly jobless claims, due at 1330 GMT, were expected to show a total of 365,000 new filings. The Philadelphia Federal Reserve Bank was due to release its December business activity survey at 1700 GMT. The index was seen down slightly to 25.4 from 25.9 in November.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031218dzci002pc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
