\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar sinks to new low vs euro in broad sell-off.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gertrude Chavez  \par \uc2 703 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2003\par 22:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Dec 17 (Reuters) - The dollar plumbed fresh lows against the euro and sank against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, undermined by positive news from Europe and still hurting from expectations that U.S. rates will remain low for some time.  \par \par \uc2 The euro broke through the psychologically important $1.2400 level, reaching a record $1.2418 earlier in the session, before trading back down to $1.2397. This is the 12th record high of the past 14 trading sessions for the euro, which has surged almost 19 percent this year.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar's fall was a combination of a few things. The tax package that came out of Germany was a slight positive even though some people were slightly disappointed with the size of the tax cut. But nonetheless, Germany is actually doing something and that's really good," said Andrew Busch, global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BMO Nesbitt Burns in Chicago.  \par \par \uc2 German newspapers reported on Wednesday that the landmark German tax and welfare reform deal agreed this week will produce over 1 billion euros more in tax relief next year than earlier announced.  \par \par \uc2 Busch also said Tuesday's weaker-than-expected consumer prices still weighed on the greenback, as the data suggested that inflation is quite tame and as a consequence U.S. interest rates will stay at their currently low level for quite some time.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar index slipped to a seven-year low of about 87.79 on Wednesday as market sentiment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained bearish. The index , a measure of the dollar against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was trading at 87.94.  \par \par \uc2 Despite a quiet trading day, the dollar posted substantial downward moves moves against most of its major counterparts. Analysts say that as the end of the year approaches, the market tends to become illiquid, so any moves could jolt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the greenback fell slightly to 107.44 yen , with traders on the alert of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The dollar hit a seven-year low against the Swiss franc of 1.2514 francs , before edging up to 1.2542 francs, down 0.4 percent on the day.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling climbed for a second straight day to an 11-year high of $1.7667 before drifting back to $1.7655.  \par \par \uc2 ECB'S ISSING SAYS EURO RATE BACK TO NORMAL  \par \par \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chief Economist Otmar Issing was quoted on Wednesday as saying the euro's exchange rate against the dollar was back to normal, having reached the same level as around the time of its introduction of $1.17 in 1999.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts also said one factor contributing to the euro's rise was a report from Market News International citing unidentified ECB sources saying the bank would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless the euro rose above $1.35.  \par \par \uc2 "Things were relatively quiet this morning until this story came out suggesting from ECB sources that they did not see the need for any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless the euro got to $1.35, and of course, whenever you put a number out there, the markets get very excited," said Robert Sinche, global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Citibank in New York.  \par \par \uc2 A spokesman for the ECB declined to comment on the report, following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's standard policy not to comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets or on reports about possible market action.  \par \par \uc2 But still the surging euro has provoked concern among European companies that export to the United States, citing the negative impact of the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength on their bottom lines.  \par \par \uc2 The co-chief executive of Airbus parent EADS said the company would have to take radical new cost-cutting measures and put additional pressure on suppliers if the euro rose to the $1.30-$1.35 level for a lengthy period of time.  \par \par \uc2 The Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, made a surprise rate cut of 25 basis points to a record low 2.25 percent, sending the Norwegian crown to a six-week low against the euro of 8.2668 crowns , and dropping it to 6.7061 crowns against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Manuela Badawy).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031217dzch003ij\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
