\par\par \b \uc2 Euro Breaks Above $1.24 As Dollar Selloff Continues  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Tom Barkley and Jamie McGeever  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 546 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2003\par 18:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The euro broke to fresh all-time highs above $1.24 as the broad selloff in the dollar continued Wednesday afternoon.  \par \par \uc2 A market source at a U.S. bank said a big option was taken out at that key level, which helped push the euro to a new high around $1.2420.  \par \par \uc2 "People were defending the option knockout, but that got taken out," the source said. "A lot of people are looking to call a top, but it's just not happening."  \par \par \uc2 The dollar also fell to a fresh 11-year low against the U.K. pound around $1.7665, as well as a seven-year low against the Swiss franc around CHF1.2514.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar has been in a sharp retreat during the North American session, following the publication of a newswire report that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the euro's appreciation is unlikely for a while yet.  \par \par \uc2 The report from Market News, quoting unnamed ECB sources, said that as long as the euro's appreciation remains orderly, there will be no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  until the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits $1.35. The ECB declined to comment on this report.  \par \par \uc2 Wednesday afternoon, the euro was trading around $1.2410, up a from $1.2325 late Tuesday in New York. It was also at Y133.14, up from Y132.52.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was at Y107.25, below Y107.49 late Tuesday, and was at CHF1.2519, down from CHF1.2600. Sterling was trading at $1.7644, up from $1.7537 late Tuesday in New York.  \par \par \uc2 The euro should face its next resistance around $1.2450 to $1.2560, according to a dealer at a Japanese bank in New York.  \par \par \uc2 The dealer said that "$1.25 is just around the corner," adding that with the market "getting thinner and thinner, anything really goes."  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the dollar has held up fairly well against the yen. Traders have cited fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as providing some support, but so far there are no clear signs of official bids from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 A trader from another Japanese bank in New York says there has been some good buying of the euro against the yen by German participants, so "it seems to be more than just funny bids."  \par \par \uc2 Still, he expects the BOJ to defend Y107, where stops are said to be set.  \par \par \uc2 According to international financial sources, Japan's government is preparing to increase by Y61 trillion the amount of money it can spend on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fight against an unwanted yen rise.  \par \par \uc2 Tokyo will seek to boost the borrowing limit on its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account by Y21 trillion this fiscal year ending March, and by another Y40 trillion next fiscal year, sources said. This year alone, authorities have sold more than Y17 trillion - a record amount - to try and halt the yen's rise.  \par \par \uc2 -By Tom Barkley, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-4385  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     tom.barkley@dowjones.com \par    -By Jamie McGeever, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-2096; jamie.mcgeever@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Miyako Takebe in Tokyo contributed to this story.)  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020031217dzch00026\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
