\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Falls To New Record Low Against Euro  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Lisa Twaronite  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 738 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2003\par 06:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar fell to a new record low against the euro Tuesday in Asia, as U.S. and European fund buying triggered stop loss orders.  \par \par \uc2 In thin afternoon trade, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  easily breezed above the old record high set overnight, tripping stops at $1.2330, and got as far as $1.2355 on the EBS trading system, market participants said.  \par \par \uc2 "At these levels, there's no historical resistance, so some players must think, 'the trend is my friend' and are pushing it higher," toward a large options-related barrier said to lie at $1.2400, a trader at an Asian bank in Tokyo said.  \par \par \uc2 Barclays Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  director Tadahiko Nashimoto predicted the euro could rise as high as $1.2475 perhaps as early as later Tuesday, and could aim for $1.2500 by early next year.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the dollar stuck to an extremely narrow Y107.56-Y107.83 range, sandwiched between Japanese exporter sales above and expectations of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  below.  \par \par \uc2 The BOJ unanimously voted to hold monetary policy steady for the third consecutive time Tuesday, judging that the country's recovering economy doesn't need extra stimulus. The decision also indicates that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't concerned about the impact on Japanese exports of the yen's rise in recent months.  \par \par \uc2 As the decision was in line with market expectations, it didn't have a direct impact on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y107.75, above Y107.57 in New York but below Y108.10 in Tokyo late Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2344, higher than $1.2305 in New York and $1.2198 in Tokyo. Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y133.01, compared with Y132.43 in New York and Y131.86 in Tokyo Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.7468, compared with $1.7456 in New York and $1.7430 in Tokyo Monday.  \par \par \uc2 In October, the bank eased policy by raising its account balance target ceiling, and BOJ governor Toshihiko Fukui acknowledged that the yen's recent surge was one reason for that step.  \par \par \uc2 So far this year, Japanese financial authorities have sold more than Y17 trillion to stem yen strength and support the country's export-led economic recovery.  \par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, market participants estimate that the aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has continued, and have speculated that the ministry could soon hit the cumulative Y79 trillion ceiling on the amount of funds it can borrow to finance \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Tuesday morning, Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs, Zembei Mizoguchi, told reporters \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will make sure it doesn't run out of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds and continues to stand ready to take appropriate steps.  \par \par \uc2 Mizoguchi declined to offer specifics on how the MOF will replenish its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds.  \par \par \uc2 Research firm 4Cast estimated that given \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in October, it may have accounted for close to 90% of the total net inflows of $27.65 billion into U.S. securities that month, compared to estimated October net private inflows as low as $3 billion.  \par \par \uc2 Such figures would underscore the extent to which the U.S. indirectly relies on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy to help offset some of its massive current account deficit. That may help explain why U.S. official rhetoric only criticizes market manipulation in general without coming down too hard Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in particular.  \par \par \uc2 Later Tuesday, the U.S. will release third-quarter data on its current account, a wider measure of U.S. international trade that includes goods and services as well as investment flows and foreign aid.  \par \par \uc2 The current account deficit is expected to narrow only modestly to $136.2 billion from a record $138.7 billion in both the first and second quarters - still an estimated 4.9% of gross domestic product.  \par \par \uc2 -By Lisa Twaronite, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; lisa.twaronite@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Bennett Richardson  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \par \par \uc2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX  \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031216dzcg0004s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
