\par\par \b \uc2 TECHNICALS- \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  market views and key levels.  \b0\par\par\uc2 611 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 2003\par 17:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     NEW YORK, Dec 12 (Reuters) - Following is a selection of\par comments from analysts on important technical developments in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par     KEITH RAPHAEL, PRESIDENT, CROSSCURRENTS INVESTMENT\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ADVISORY:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 - EURO/DOLLAR: "I don't see any improvement in the  \par \par \uc2 broad-based dollar picture. You will still see further erosion  \par \par \uc2 of the dollar. The euro will continue to try to test the  \par \par \uc2 $1.2305 November 1998 high and remain in a short-term range  \par \par \uc2 between $1.2100 and $1.2300. If we exceeded that range, that's  \par \par \uc2 the only way we would see acceleration of 2 percent, in either  \par \par \uc2 direction, to $1.2525 or $1.1935."  \par \par \uc2 - STERLING/DOLLAR: "Closed last month and last week above  \par \par \uc2 $1.7110 and that was a bullish indication for rally to $1.7790  \par \par \uc2 over a two week view. Support levels: $1.7310 is a strong pivot  \par \par \uc2 point which I doubt we will see today. (Another support level  \par \par \uc2 lies at) $1.7350."  \par \par \uc2 - DOLLAR/YEN: "Still looks very vulnerable. I think (the  \par \par \uc2 dollar) will continue to try to grind (below) through 106.60  \par \par \uc2 yen to 104.80 yen into early January despite covert  \par \par \uc2 (yen-weakening) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ). On the upside, right  \par \par \uc2 now, the bigger cap (for the dollar) is 110.90 yen, but more  \par \par \uc2 shorter term is at 108.95 yen."  \par \par \uc2 TOM FITZPATRICK, CHIEF TECHNICAL ANALYST, CITIBANK:  \par \par \uc2 - DOLLAR INDEX: "Last week's fall of the dollar index  \par \par \uc2 below 1998 lows suggested we were in for further significant  \par \par \uc2 dollar losses.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "(The key levels are): euro/dollar at $1.2226, dollar/Swiss\par francs of 1.2740 francs, the Australian dollar at US$0.7410 and\par sterling at $1.7366...our belief being if we sustain breaks (of\par the dollar weakening through) those levels on a weekly close\par basis, which we could very well do today....that would suggest\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 another depreciation of the dollar by at least 10 percent."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - DOLLAR/YEN: "Is still trading in a world of its own.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There is a negative bias, but in the real world we have to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 accept it is not really trading freely. We will see (the dollar  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 vs the yen) push lower, but it looks like at a slower pace than  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may push up against the dollar."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - EURO/YEN: "The 132.85 yen (level): if we were to break  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 above that...the euro/yen could find its way all the way back  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to 140.90 yen. The first support level is on 130.30 yen."  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 10:49 a.m. EST (1549GMT). All data taken  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 from Reuters calculated from the levels at 4:30 p.m. EST (2130  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GMT) in the previous New York session.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Last     US Close  %      YTD %   2002\par                               11 Dec.  Change  Change  Close\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par Euro/dlr             1.2245   1.2209   +0.29  +17.33   1.0436\par Dlr/yen              107.8