\par\par \b \uc2 BOJ Watch: Policy Shift Unlikely Despite Yen's Rise  \b0\par\par\uc2 854 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2003\par 07:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Hiroshi Inoue \par  \par    A Dow Jones Newswires Column \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Bank of Japan policy makers will likely leave monetary settings steady for a third consecutive time when they meet Monday and Tuesday despite recent yen strength that threatens to crimp exports.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 The BOJ's nine board members don't believe the yen's gains against the dollar are yet significant enough to rock the foundations of Japan's so far modest recovery, say people close to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to a more than three-year low of Y106.74 against the yen Wednesday before heavy yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  amounting to an estimated Y1 trillion pushed the dollar over one yen higher. At 0612 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y108.18. \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is the responsibility of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which acts in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets via the BOJ.  \par \par \uc2 Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yen remains slightly higher against the dollar than it was when the BOJ policy board last met on Nov. 21 and is up 10% against the greenback since the start of August.  \par \par \uc2 A fall in the dollar below Y100 "would be problematic for Japan's economy," said a person close to the BOJ. "But the yen's rise so far isn't viewed as likely to worsen the economy."  \par \par \uc2 Not only does the BOJ believe the yen's rise so far won't jeopardize the recovery but a number of board members continue to believe that flooding Japan's financial system with more cash than is currently washing through financial markets wouldn't boost economic activity or stop the yen's rise.  \par \par \uc2 "Some members still maintain the view that there is no clear mechanism to increase the account balance target so as to boost economic activity and weaken the yen," said another source.  \par \par \uc2 Still, the volatile yen and recently volatile stock prices remain key risk factors for the economy, he said.  \par \par \uc2 "Stock prices are slightly low compared with the current solid state of the economy," he added. The Nikkei 225 Stock Average ended Thursday 1.7% higher at 10075.14 but is 10% below a recent peak of 11238.63 set on Oct. 21.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  already anchors short-term interest rates near zero and targets liquidity, which it measures through the current account balance, in a range between Y27 trillion and Y32 trillion.  \par \par \uc2 The board last eased policy on Oct. 10 when it raised the top of its liquidity target range by Y2 trillion from Y30 trillion. Many analysts at the time said the BOJ increased its liquidity target to allow it to continue yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  without having to always drain yen funds from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's domestic money markets.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par      Tankan Likely To Back Steady Policy \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Financial markets aren't expecting further monetary policy action anytime soon.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Despite the yen's rise, there is no imminent need for the BOJ to take action right now," said Susumu Kato, chief fixed-income strategist at Lehman Brothers.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BOJ has since Oct. 14 maintained its account balance around Y30 trillion so it could boost liquidity toward the top of its range if necessary.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The yen has risen but the BOJ will leave monetary policy steady," said Yasunari Ueno, chief market economist at Mizuho Securities. "The BOJ doesn't need to take action because there is room for the BOJ to cope with the yen's rise under the current policy framework."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's December Tankan survey due Friday is likely to add to expectations that further monetary policy action isn't necessary. Economists expect the survey will show optimists outnumbered pessimists among Japan's large manufacturers for the second quarter in a row and that the yen's rise so far hasn't hurt corporate profits or investment plans given exports and production remain strong.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Regardless of the yen's rise over the past three months, the Tankan survey will show improvement in corporate sentiment and business plans, given stronger exports and production," said one of the sources.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In fact, some people close to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  say the BOJ believes the economy is performing in line with, if not better than, its Oct. 31 semiannual outlook report, which said the economy will gain cyclical momentum for a recovery in the second half of the current fiscal year.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The economy is basically in line with the standard view...but hope is increasing of a sustainable economic recovery on the back of a stronger-than-expected global recovery," said a source close to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some officials at the BOJ are perplexed why some market participants remain bearish on the economy's outlook given recently strong economic data, he added. "I hope the tankan result will slightly modify market players' pessimistic economic view," he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By Hiroshi Inoue, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-9203; hiroshi.inoue@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Hiroshi Inoue, a correspondent for Dow Jones Newswires in Tokyo, has covered the Bank of Japan for a dozen years and also looks at credit markets.)  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Bennett Richardson  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1042 4131  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031211dzcb0004u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
