\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones News Highlights Top Stories Of The Day  \b0\par\par\uc2 974 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2003\par 14:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GE TO BUY IKON ASSETS FOR $1.5B \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GE Vendor Financial agrees to pay $1.5 billion for IKON's $1.8 billion leasing portfolio and agrees to offer jobs to about 400 IKON employees and provide it with funding or servicing of its lease originations in the U.S. and Canada.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ALLIANCE SET TO CUT FEES UNDER PROPOSED SETTLEMENT   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Alliance Capital, one of largest publicly traded mutual-fund companies in U.S., offers to cut annual fees it charges investors for managing its mutual funds as part of proposed settlement with New York attorney general's office for improper trading.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RETAIL SALES SEEN UP, JOBLESS CLAIMS DOWN   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Economists look for an increase of 0.7% in total retail sales in November, but for more modest 0.3% rise in non-auto sales. Jobless claims filed in week ended Dec. 6 expected to show decrease by 5,000, to 360,000.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DANAHER OFFERS $730M FOR RADIOMETER   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tools and testing-equipment maker Danaher offers to buy Danish blood gas analysis instrument maker Radiometer for about $75.20 a share. Radiometer's board has approved the offer, and its main shareholder has agreed to accept it.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FRENCH PM SAYS CLOSE TO EXECUTIVE LIFE DEAL   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Government close to reaching a deal with U.S. federal prosecutors that covers all the companies and persons involved in the case. Spokesman confirms the state will be paying no more than the $475 million previously agreed.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIP MORRIS APPEALS 'LIGHTS' CASE   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philip Morris USA files initial appellate brief with Illinois Supreme Court, seeking reversal of $10.1 billion verdict in class action case. In March, Madison County judge ruled Altria unit deceived Illinois purchasers.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB SAYS EURO-ZONE GDP UP 0.4% IN 2003   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Lower than 0.7% growth it forecast six months ago. Leaves 2004 growth unchanged at 1.6%, accelerating to 2.4% in 2005. Substantially raises HICP to 1.8% from 1.3% forecast in June.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROPEAN STOCKS MOSTLY HIGHER   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shares in London buck trend and trade lower following profit warning from Matalan, which pulls retailers down. Shares in Paris and Frankfurt modestly higher.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOKYO SHARES END HIGHER   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nikkei 225 Stock Average regains key 10000 mark as yen's fall against dollar sparks bargain-hunting of shares in exporters such as Honda Motor and Canon.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AT&T TO LAUNCH INTERNET PHONE SERVICE   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Joins rush of companies planning to offer consumers phone service using Internet technology, allowing it to sell cheaper local and long-distance service without having to rent local-phone lines from regional Bells.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GOODYEAR FINDS ACCOUNTING ISSUES IN EUROPE   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Amid grappling with errors in its internal billing system in the U.S., discovery could spell trouble with its union as it postpones SEC filing of restated results until sometime next year, and also casts shadow over its turnaround plans.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KPMG IS ACCUSED OF DELAY TACTICS   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Justice Department says company improperly withheld documents from the IRS to hide tax-sheltering activity, signaling the government's increasing frustration with what it considers delaying tactics by the accounting firm.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US HELICOPTER CRASH CAUSED BY GROUND FIRE   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An Apache helicopter that crash-landed near the northern Iraqi city of Mosul yesterday may have been hit by ground fire while making a low pass over the area, U.S. soldiers say.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTEL TO COMBINE COMMUNICATIONS GROUPS   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Announces major restructuring of struggling communications efforts, after embarrassing $600 million write-off in wireless chip business.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AHOLD RIGHTS ISSUE 94.6% SUBSCRIBED   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Offering $3.7 billion in 587.3 million new shares which will start trading Dec. 17, quelling some fears in market that it would receive lukewarm response. Shares gain 1%.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PARMALAT PLUMMETS AS TRADING RESUMES   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shares of Italian dairy products company fall as much as 50% as trading finally gets under way, with 23 million shares changing hands in first eight minutes as investors rush for exit.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TWO PAKISTAN NUCLEAR SCIENTISTS QUESTIONED   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Former director general at the country's top nuclear laboratory is among those arrested in connection with alleged links with Iran's nuclear program. Pakistan has been accused of sharing its technological know-how.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HEALTHSOUTH EXEC GETS PRISON TIME; \par FOUR OFFICIALS PUT ON PROBATION   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal judge sentences former assistant controller Emery Harris to five months in federal prison, while four lower-level accounting officials receive four-year probation terms. All five agree to cooperate with wide-ranging criminal probe.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WAL-MART BIDS FOR SAFEWAY STORES   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Group's U.K. chain Asda approaches with an offer to buy 70 of its stores for nearly GBP2 billion, according to people familiar with the situation. Move aimed at taking the wind out of an imminent takeover offer by William Morrison.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GLAXO, BOERINGER LET AFRICA MAKE AIDS GENERICS   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Following legal pressure from activists groups agree to allow more generic versions of their patented AIDS medicines to be made in South Africa and other sub-Saharan countries, a move that could lower costs in the area.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par   ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARIES ======= \par  \par CHARTING MARKETS \par Dollar To Rally Against Yen   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Technical levels unchanged, with market testing bottom somewhere between first support of 107.46 and second support of 107.00. Strong corrective rally may be imminent.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FOCUS \par Dollar's Little Help From A Friend   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  standing by to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the dollar has a better chance of resisting selling pressure. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent bout of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is not only boosting the dollar against the yen but helping to keep it up against the euro.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   ============ U.S. MARKETS ACTION =========== \par DJIA              9921.86 from Wednesday. \par NASDAQ            1904.65 from Wednesday. \par S&P 500           1059.05 from Wednesday. \par 10-year T-note    down 6/32 at 99 8/32 yield 4.341 \par NYMEX Spot Crude  down $0.05 at $31.84/bbl \par Dollar/Euro       down 0.0057 at 1.2158 \par  \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 5030 55101  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020031211dzcb0002v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
