\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX - G7 policymakers' recent  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  comments.  \b0\par\par\uc2 940 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2003\par 18:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Dec 11 (Reuters) - Most Group of Seven policymakers in recent weeks have said little to temper the slide of the U.S. dollar against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The dollar on Thursday recovered a little ground after hitting hit fresh record lows earlier this week against the euro and three-year lows against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Here is a summary of recent remarks by leading politicians and central bankers about the recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves:  \par \par \uc2 JOHN SNOW - U.S. Treasury Secretary  \par \par \uc2 December 10 - "Our policy with respect to the dollar is to continue to emphasize the strong dollar," Snow said in an interview with the cable television channel CNBC. "It's in our national interest and I've reaffirmed that over and over again."  \par \par \uc2 "We think the exchange value of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is best set in open and competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets where \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are kept to a minimum," Snow said.  \par \par \uc2 ERNST WELTEKE - European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governing Council member and president of the Bundesbank.  \par \par \uc2 December 10 - "The euro's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate is not far removed from its long-term average and that is why there should be no major consequences for competition."  \par \par \uc2 Asked by reporters after the Bundesbank's annual news conference whether the euro was appreciating too rapidly, Welteke said: "We know markets tend to overshoot, but I do not see this in the current situation."  \par \par \uc2 RAGHURAM RAJAN - International Monetary Fund Chief Economist  \par \par \uc2 December 10 - "The possibility for central banks to be effective in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets has decreased in the recent years," he said in a Handlesblatt newspaper interview. He also said downward pressure on the dollar would ease "over the medium term" as faster growth in Asia and Europe helped reduce the U.S. current account deficit.  \par \par \uc2 MARIO BALDASSARI - Italian Deputy Economy Minister:  \par \par \uc2 December 9 - "At $1.21-1.22, the euro is too strong and is penalising the European recovery," he said in a newspaper interview. "Why do the two most powerful economic regions in the world abandon their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the free fluctuation of markets instead of trying to defend a dollar parity of between $0.9 and $1.1 versus the euro, a level adequate to guarantee the stability of the international system?"  \par \par \uc2 SADAKAZU TANIGAKI - Japanese Finance Minister.  \par \par \uc2 December 9 - "Current movements are somewhat different from fundamentals," Tanigaki told reporters after market participants said they suspected Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  upon which he refused to comment. "The dollar was trading at 107.15-20 yen just now and the market seems to have been moving rather rapidly."  \par \par \uc2 HEIZO TAKENAKA - Japanese Economics and Financial Services Minister  \par \par \uc2 December 9 - "We're looking at the trend in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates over the medium term but sharp fluctuations have an impact on corporate sentiment," he told a news conference.  \par \par \uc2 JOHN SNOW - U.S. Treasury Secretary:  \par \par \uc2 December 8 - "Of course, our policy on the dollar also has been articulated over and over - we favour a strong dollar and we feel that \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' exchange value is best set in open, competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets where demand and supply forces are allowed to play out," he said in a Reuters interview.  \par \par \uc2 ZEMBEI MIZOGUCHI - Japanese vice finance minister for international affairs  \par \par \uc2 December 8 - "There are some moves targeting a weak dollar in the market. But as I have said before, the relative strength of the U.S. economy has not changed.....We will take necessary measures if the moves go too far."  \par \par \uc2 WOLFGANG CLEMENT - German economy minister  \par \par \uc2 December 8 - "No, that has not been the case to date," Clement said in Berlin when asked by journalists if the euro's rise to record levels just below $1.22 had hurt exports.  \par \par \uc2 JEAN-CLAUDE TRICHET - ECB President  \par \par \uc2 December 4 - "I will not comment on day to day and week to week evolution of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on markets. I will not embark on such comments....I've already said that we are pursuing - all the central banks in the world we are pursuing - long-term strategies that are aiming at delivering stable and strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said at the monthly ECB news conference.  \par \par \uc2 FRANCIS MER - French Finance Minister:  \par \par \uc2 December 4 - "The movements taking place now are certainly not in the hands of central banks but in those of the markets."  \par \par \uc2 CAIO KOCH-WESER, German Deputy Finance Minister  \par \par \uc2 December 4 - "The euro should not bear the burden of adjustment alone," Koch-Weser told reporters on the margins of a banking conference in Munich, when asked about the dollar's weakness.  \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is always possible, but is something one doesn't talk about (publicly)," he added.  \par \par \uc2 JUERGEN STARK - Bundesbank Vice President:  \par \par \uc2 December 2 - "The present exchange rate of the euro versus the U.S. dollar is not exceptional. It's slightly above the long-term average of the dollar/mark" exchange rate over the last few years.  \par \par \uc2 JEAN-CLAUDE TRICHET - ECB President  \par \par \uc2 "You will not be surprised when I tell you that I never comment and will never comment day to day over short term evolutions on the exchange markets on the floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ... I have nothing to add to that apart from the fact that we meet regularly within the G3/G7 and we have occasions for saying regularly that we are very keen on continuing to cooperate at a global level," Trichet told the European Parliament.  \par \par \uc2 PEDRO SOLBES - European Economics and Monetary Affairs Commissioner:  \par \par \uc2 December 1 - "We are following the euro rate. The exchange rate is defined by markets. We are more worried by volatility than by the level of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 ** For story on the hands-off approach senior U.S. and European policymakers have taken in public to the tumbling dollar,.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031211dzcb003br\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
