\par\par \b \uc2 GLOBAL MARKETS-Dollar steady, stocks hold gains after U.S. data.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Nigel Stephenson  \par \uc2 532 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2003\par 15:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Dec 11 (Reuters) - The dollar stayed firm against the euro on Thursday and European stocks held their small gains after stronger than expected U.S. retail sales data.  \par \par \uc2 However Wall Street was seen opening flat after an unexpected rise in weekly jobless claims took the shine off the sales report.  \par \par \uc2 The Commerce Department said sales rose 0.9 percent in November, boosted by auto and electronics sales, exceeding Wall Street expectations for a 0.7 percent rise. Jobless claims rose by 13,000 to 378,000, the highest level in six weeks.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. stock index futures         were marginally down after the data,\par indicating a flat start.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European shares held their earlier gains on upbeat comments from semiconductor maker STMicroelectronics (STM.PA) and after the drop in the euro against the dollar boosted car makers.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The euro is below $1.22...That's probably why autos are up," said Joerg Kraemer, chief strategist at Invesco Asset Management.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Italian foodmaker Parmalat (PRFI.MI) plunged 50 percent as a three-day trading suspension was lifted.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The FTSE Eurotop 300 index  was 0.1 percent higher and the narrower DJ\par Euro STOXX 50 index             was up 0.11 percent.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese stocks rose, with the main index topping 10,000, as exporters prospering after suspected Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday sent the yen lower against the greenback.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese car makers and other exporters were lifted by the weaker yen.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The Bank of Japan sold the yen and the market has welcomed that," said Masaru Ueda, head of investment strategy at Marusan Securities. "But with foreigners mostly out of the market ahead of Christmas, it does not really have much more momentum than a technical rebound."   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Nikkei index  closed 1.66 percent higher at 10,075.14 points while\par the broader TOPIX index         ended up 1.06 percent.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DOLLAR LIFTS OFF LOWS  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar was half a percent firmer against the euro at $1.2158, compared with Tuesday's record low around $1.2276.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was last at 108.32 yen , steady on the New York close but 1.5 yen above a three-year low hit on Tuesday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks closed lower on Wednesday as investors took profits and remained cautious ahead of the retail sales data.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Dow Jones industrial average  fell 0.02 percent and the\par technology-dominated Nasdaq         shed 0.19 percent.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Euro zone government bond yields stayed higher after the data. "It is a bit of a mixed bag," said Audrey Childe-Freeman, European economist at CIBC World Markets. "You have to find some encouragement from the retail sales data, which shows that there is still life in the U.S. consumer sector."   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The two-year German Schatz yield  was 1.8 basis points higher at 2.68\par percent, compared with a 2.875 percent high struck on December 1, while\par the 10-year Bund             yield was 2.3 basis points higher at 4.38\par percent.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There was little reaction to European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  forecasts which saw higher euro zone inflation in 2004 but kept the bank's growth outlook unchanged.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031211dzcb0023h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
