\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar keeps firm tone vs euro.  \b0\par\par\uc2 227 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2003\par 08:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In LONDON item headlined "Dollar keeps firm tone vs euro in\par  early Europe" please read in second paragraph "But at $1.2169\par  per euro ... instead of "But at $1.2269 per euro" (corrects\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 price)  \f28 \par \par \uc2 A corrected repition follows  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Dec 11 (Reuters) - The dollar firmed against the euro on Thursday and held steady on the yen after suspected yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the previous session helped stop the greenback's broad slide.  \par \par \uc2 But at $1.2169 per euro it was barely a cent above record lows against the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and it was within two yen of three year lows against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with little hope of escaping the current account deficit worries that have weakened it.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 0740 GMT, the dollar was nearly half a percent higher against the\par euro. On Tuesday it hit record lows against the euro for the eighth day\par in a row. The dollar was flat on the yen at 108.22  and nearly half a\par percent higher on the Swiss franc       .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monthly report is due at 0900 GMT.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. initial jobless claims are due at 1330 GMT and are expected to show 360,000 new filings. Disappointing jobless figures last Friday weighed heavily on the greenback. U.S. retail sales are also due at 1330 GMT.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031211dzcb001gm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\pics