\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED- \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar firms after suspected BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 796 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 2003\par 23:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 In NEW YORK story headlined "\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -Dollar firms after    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  suspected BOJ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," please read in second paragraph\par  ... "The dollar surged by more than 1 percent to a session high\par  around 108.73 yen..."  instead of ... "...a session high of\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 around $108.73 yen." (Corrects to drop dollar sign).   \par \par \uc2 A corrected version follows.   \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices)   \par \par \uc2 By Manuela Badawy   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Dec 10 (Reuters) - The dollar pushed higher from three-year lows against the yen and a record low against the euro late on Wednesday, reversing its losing streak on yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar surged by more than 1 percent to a session high around 108.73 yen early on Wednesday as dealers estimated the BOJ may have bought up to $5 billion, or roughly 540 billion yen in covert action, even though there was no official confirmation from Tokyo.   \par \par \uc2 However, the dollar softened back to trade near 108.44 yen, a 1.20 percent increase on the day.   \par \par \uc2 "We saw some dollar buying against the yen aggressively due to BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  today. They took (the dollar) up from levels from about 107.25 yen all the way up to 108.75 yen. The euro gained also on the back of the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Chris Romano, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at GAIN Capital, an online \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading firm in Warren, New Jersey.   \par \par \uc2 The Nikkei News service said in a report that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could have amounted for as much as 1 trillion yen.   \par \par \uc2 "This has been the first aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  we have seen from the BOJ in a couple of weeks. There is a possibility they could come in again this evening. They do like to take advantage sometimes of illiquid markets being that it's December and it's toward the end of the year," Romano said.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar hit a three-year low below 107 yen on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 The euro gave up some gains after climbing more than 1 percent to a high of 132.69 yen .   \par \par \uc2 The greenback had been edging higher in Asian trade after the U.S. Federal Reserve stuck with its pledge to keep monetary policy easy "for a considerable period" on Tuesday but dropped its concern about falling prices.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar rose 0.43 percent against the Swiss franc to 1.2669  francs,\par and was steady at C$1.3079       against the Canadian dollar. The\par Australian dollar was down 0.38 percent at around US$0.7385\par against the U.S. dollar.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The greenback rebounded from a fresh 11-year low against sterling of $1.7477 . This is cable's best showing since October 1992, a few weeks after Black Wednesday, when Britain left Europe's Exchange Rate Mechanism.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cable refers to the exchange rate between the U.S. dollar and the British pound sterling.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AND ON THE NINTH DAY...   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After eight straight sessions of record highs against the dollar, the euro rally paused. It fell to $1.2213 , loss of 0.4 percent on the day after reaching a record $1.2276 on Tuesday, according to Reuters data.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governing Council member Ernst Welteke said the euro is near its long-term average value and this should not harm the competitiveness of European firms.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We know markets tend to over-shoot, but I do not see this in the current situation," Welteke told reporters.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Welteke also said interest rates in the euro zone - currently 2 percent - are likely to stay at their record lows for a considerable time, mirroring the language of the Fed.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Elsewhere, Saudi Arabian Oil Minister Ali al-Naimi told reporters on Wednesday he remained concerned over the low level of the dollar, but said fresh gains in oil prices were justified given the greenback's weakness.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DOWNWARD SPIRAL   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Before Wednesday, Japan was thought to have thrown almost 18 trillion yen ($168 billion) at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets this year in a bid to prevent a strengthening yen from choking off the country's export-led recovery.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki declined comment on whether the authorities had acted but dealers said Tokyo might have wanted to calm foreign exchanges after the dollar's string of lows threatened to turn its fall into a rout.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An advisory panel to Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi said the economy was still in a mild deflationary state but there were some signs of change.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There has been market speculation \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is close to its allotted ceiling for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  funds. But a top \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official told Reuters there had been no problem with raising funds via three-month finance bills and he saw no need to use longer maturity debt.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Daniel Bases in New York and Charlotte Cooper in London).    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031211dzca0017m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
