\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr/Yen Edges Down On Strong Machinery Orders  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Ron Harui  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 771 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 2003\par 07:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar edged down against the yen in Asia Tuesday as robust Japanese economic data sparked speculator-led selling, though the U.S. unit found solid support in the low-Y107s from what was thought to be buying by Japanese authorities.  \par \par \uc2 After Japan's core machinery orders posted a much stronger-than-expected rise of 17.4% on month in October, speculators dumped the dollar to test the Japanese Finance Ministry's resolve to curb the yen's resurgence.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts surveyed by Dow Jones Newswires and Nikkei News had estimated on average that core machinery orders grew 4.9% from September.  \par \par \uc2 But the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide was limited by apparent yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese authorities just above the psychologically key Y107 level. And dealers say the authorities may continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  later in the session.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday failed to provide funds through Friday despite expected deficits in banks' account balance at the BOJ over the next couple of days, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 Market participants interpreted this inaction as a sign of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's intention to leave room for more yen selling in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market either later Tuesday or Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Sentiment on the dollar could worsen a bit if the U.S. Federal Open Market Committee decides at its meeting later in the global day to leave unchanged the wording of its commitment to keep interest rates low for a "considerable period," a position it first set out in its August report.  \par \par \uc2 That could spur foreign capital outflows from the U.S. as investors would likely continue to favor higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  than the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 At 0530 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y107.23, below Y107.34 late Monday in New York. The dollar was at Y107.63 late Monday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2226, higher than $1.2224 late Monday in New York. The euro was at $1.2153 in Tokyo Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y131.09, down from Y131.20 in New York late Monday. The euro was at Y130.84 in Tokyo late Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.7345, up from $1.7331 in New York and higher than $1.7277 in Tokyo Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Seeking to cast cold water on the yen's latest surge, Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said Tuesday the yen's climb to a fresh three-year high of Y107.11 to the dollar overnight was out of step with economic fundamentals.  \par \par \uc2 "We continue to believe that the U.S. economy is on a solid footing," he said. "Current movements (in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) are contrary to fundamentals."  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki's remarks were a strong hint that the ministry has been active in the market, given its standing policy to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the yen rises too quickly or diverges too far from the levels it believes are warranted by economic conditions.  \par \par \uc2 Banking and Economy Minister Heizo Takenaka also joined the chorus of top Japanese government officials warning against a sharp yen rise.  \par \par \uc2 "Rapid, unstable fluctuations affect corporate sentiment, and from that viewpoint, it is my understanding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will take steps as necessary," Takenaka said earlier in the session.  \par \par \uc2 But he also sought to downplay the impact of the yen's recent rise, saying short-term movements won't affect the economy, which remains on a steady recovery path.  \par \par \uc2 Revised gross domestic product data released early Tuesday showed Japan's economy grew more slowly than originally thought in the July-September quarter, as the pace of business spending dropped.  \par \par \uc2 The nation's economy grew 0.3% in the three months through September compared with a preliminary estimate of 0.6% growth, as corporate capital expenditures in the period rose just 0.5%, compared with a preliminary rise of 2.8%.  \par \par \uc2 Many private economists had expected weaker growth after a \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  survey showed capital investment in the third quarter rose 0.4% on year, a much smaller pace than a jump of 6.4% in the previous survey.  \par \par \uc2 -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2942; ron.harui@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Kirsty Mackenzie  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \par \par \uc2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX  \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031209dzc90005y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
