\par\par \b \uc2 ODJ OUTLOOK 04: Dlr To Flirt With Y100 On US C/A, Japan Econ  \b0\par\par\uc2 1,046 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 2003\par 16:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 DJCS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par (Repeating) \par  \par    By Ron Harui \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \par  \par   TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The yen, already around three-year highs against the \par dollar, is expected to push higher in 2004 as a yawning U.S. trade deficit and \par a recovering Japanese economy push the U.S. unit down near Y100. \par  \par   Although the U.S. economy is sizzling with its strongest growth in 20 years, \par financial markets are seizing on the massive current-account gap, which \par requires about $2 billion of foreign money every business day to finance. \par Moreover, despite the rebound, the Federal Reserve is widely expected to keep \par interest rates near their 45-year lows, further damping the incentive to own \par U.S. assets. \par  \par   And critically for the dollar's exchange rate against the yen, a growing \par Japanese economy may temper some of Tokyo's zeal in curbing the unruly yen, \par allowing the dollar to slide in the coming year, analysts say. \par  \par   "The weak-dollar trend is unlikely to change, and Japan's economic growth \par could beat market expectations" in 2004, said Tohru Sasaki, chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par strategist at J.P. Morgan Chase Bank in Tokyo. He expects the greenback will \par fall to Y95 by the end of next year. \par  \par   Six banks canvassed by Dow Jones Newswires see the dollar falling, on \par average, to Y101 by late 2004, with forecast lows ranging from Y95 to Y105. \par The dollar, which started 2003 at Y118.82, tumbled to Y107.06 on Tuesday, its \par lowest since November 2000. \par  \par   Around 0930 it was at Y107.26. \par  \par   The U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hasn't flirted with yen "parity" since November 1995, when \par it was recovering from that year's modern-era low of Y79. As Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par crumbled in the region's financial crisis, the dollar climbed as Y147.61 in \par 1998. This year the dollar traded up to Y121.88 in March before falling \par against the yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as part of its global weakness. \par  \par   The Japanese Finance Ministry successfully defended the dollar at Y115 from \par midyear until the U.S. convinced Japan and the rest of the Group of Seven to \par call for greater \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  flexibility - code for China, Japan and other Asian \par export powerhouses to stop weakening their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par  \par  \par    U.S. Structural Problems To Haunt Dollar In 2004 \par  \par  \par   At first blush it seems odd for the dollar to fall when the U.S. economy is \par growing at developing-country rates. The world's biggest economy expanded at \par an eye-popping annual clip of 8.2% in the third quarter. \par  \par   But that incandescent growth isn't being met at home - the U.S. is sucking \par in exports at a torrid pace, with the current-account deficit running at more \par than 5% of gross domestic product. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market is ignoring good news \par about U.S. growth and 18-month highs for share prices and focusing instead on \par America's precarious reliance on foreigners to make up for its lack of \par savings. \par  \par   Structural problems, chiefly the massive current-account and budget \par deficits, are expected to continue haunting the dollar next year. \par  \par   Huge foreign-investment flows have plugged the current-account gap so far, \par but concerns are growing that foreign investors will have less appetite for \par dollar-denominated securities with U.S. interest rates expected to remain low. \par The Bank of England and the Australian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have started what appears \par to be a global cycle of higher rates, but market participants expect the Fed \par to remain accommodative despite strong U.S. growth. \par  \par   Although the economy is growing, inflation is quiescent, with plenty of \par slack left in the economy and the labor market, in particular, still weak. \par Sasaki and other analysts think the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may keep its key policy \par rate around 1% well into 2004 and perhaps even for the entire year after a \par disappointing rise in non-farm payrolls. \par  \par   The dollar was pummeled Friday when the government reported non-farm \par payrolls rose by only 57,000 in November, well below economists' forecasts for \par a 150,000 gain. That has pushed back expectations for when the Fed will begin \par raising rates. \par  \par   "A Fed rate hike in June had been expected, but this may no longer be \par possible," said Koji Fukaya, chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at Bank of Tokyo- \par Mitsubishi. He forecasts the dollar at Y100 at the end of next year. \par  \par  \par    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Econ Recovery May Curtail MOF's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par  \par   On the other side of the dollar/yen equation, the Japanese economy is \par picking up, local stocks are in demand, and those factors may curb Tokyo's \par unprecedented campaign of yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the dollar. \par  \par   The government has upgraded its economic assessment three times in the past \par four months, saying in November the economy is "showing an incipient recovery" \par on the back of an improving global economy and higher production and consumer \par spending. Japan's GDP grew for the seventh straight quarter in the July- \par September period, at a real annual rate of 1.4%. And although it's off its \par recent highs, the benchmark Nikkei 225 Stock Average is up 33% from April's 20- \par year lows. \par  \par   Continued strength in exports and corporate capital spending will likely \par sustain the economy and rising corporate profits are expected to keep Japanese \par equities on an even keel. Welcome factors such as those may make it harder for \par the Finance Ministry to justify \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prevent "excessive" rises in \par the yen. \par  \par   The ministry sold Y17.8 trillion, mostly for dollars, through the Bank of \par Japan in the first 11 months of the year, well above its previous full-year \par record. \par  \par   "Assuming the nation's economy shows further improvements, acceptance of \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could decrease," said Toru Umemoto, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par strategist at Morgan Stanley, in a report. "Maintaining the political \par consensus on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is becoming more and more important for the MOF to \par be able to continue \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the yen." \par  \par   The U.S. and other trading partners have made it clear they will keep up the \par pressure on Asian authorities not to cheapen their own \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in a "beggar- \par thy-neighbor" policy, aimed at boosting exports, especially when economies are \par improving. \par  \par   A stronger yen makes Japanese goods more expensive or less profitable \par overseas and crimps the yen value of Japanese companies'  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCS000020031209dzc9000fy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
