\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 :Dlr Dips To New Low Vs Yen, But Bears Fear MOF  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Jonathan Soble  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 684 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 2003\par 06:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar dipped to a fresh three-year low against the yen in Asia Monday, but sellers refrained from pushing the greenback even lower amid worries \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Speculator-led sales knocked the dollar to Y107.51 in early trade, dealers said. That was just below Friday's low of Y107.53 and the dollar's weakest level against the yen since Nov. 13, 2000.  \par \par \uc2 But many dollar bears feared Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  would pull the trigger on yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  below Y107.50, and demand from Japanese banks ahead of the 0100 GMT Tokyo fixing soon pulled the dollar back near its levels late Friday.  \par \par \uc2 "Without \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the dollar could easily fall to Y105 by year's end," said Satoshi Tate, a vice president for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at UFJ Bank. "But the authorities are sure to step in before that."  \par \par \uc2 Tate predicted support from the MOF would keep the dollar above Y107 through the end of December.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities, worried that a sharp yen rise could derail the country's economic recovery by hurting exports, sold an unprecedented Y17.8 trillion in the first 11 months of the year in an effort to rein in the surging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "The key level they want to protect is Y105," said the head dealer at a European brokerage in Tokyo. "But to do that they need to step in before that, starting around the current level."  \par \par \uc2 He warned, however, that the ministry could let the dollar fall slightly below levels at which market players expect \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in order to maximize the impact of its eventual yen-selling.  \par \par \uc2 "Their recent tactic is to let (the dollar) break below a key level, then step and catch everyone short," he said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y107.63, just below Y107.67 late Friday in New York. The dollar was at Y108.31 late Friday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2153, lower than $1.2162 late Friday in New York. The euro was at $1.2081 in Tokyo Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y130.84, down from Y130.95 in New York late Friday. The euro was at Y130.88 in Tokyo late Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.7277, down from $1.7295 in New York but higher than $1.7216 in Tokyo Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's point-man on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Zembei Mizoguchi, said Tokyo would continue to take appropriate steps to counter excessive yen strength.  \par \par \uc2 Mizoguchi called the yen's upsurge a "short-term, speculative move" and reiterated the ministry's view that further gains for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be unwarranted given the strength of the U.S. economy compared with Japan's.  \par \par \uc2 The latest bout of yen strength spooked investors in Japanese equities. The benchmark Nikkei 225 Stock Average plunged nearly 330 points Monday, threatening the psychologically important 10000 mark.  \par \par \uc2 Trading ranges for the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs were narrow on the whole. The euro slipped about a tenth of a cent as players took profits on its surge to record highs versus the dollar in recent sessions.  \par \par \uc2 "The euro rise may be a bit overdone for now," said the European brokerage dealer.  \par \par \uc2 He predicted the single unit would climb at a more modest pace to around $1.22 by the end of the month, but acknowledged that his cautious view put him in the minority. "The market is looking at $1.25."  \par \par \uc2 -By Jonathan Soble, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; jonathan.soble@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by John Gibson  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \par \par \uc2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX  \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031208dzc800058\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
