\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar flat, awaiting U.S. jobs data.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Naomi Tajitsu  \par \uc2 645 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2003\par 07:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Dec 5 (Reuters) - The dollar was calm on Friday, steadying above record lows set against the euro the previous day as the market waited quietly for U.S. payroll data.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the dollar was held up by speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , seeking to limit damage to its exporters, would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell below 108 yen.  \par \par \uc2 "Basically, the markets are just waiting for the (payroll) figures," said Kazuo Watanabe, general manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Daiwa Securities SMBC.  \par \par \uc2 But doubts remained about the dollar's ability to benefit from strong job figures due later in the day, as positive U.S. data recently has been stifled by worries about U.S. current account deficits and concerns over Middle East violence.  \par \par \uc2 "Right now, the market is not too focused on fundamentals. With issues like Iraq, the focus is more on political factors," said Kosuke Hanao, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at Royal Bank of Scotland.  \par \par \uc2 "Essentially, the market is combing around for issues and figures to move on."  \par \par \uc2 U.S. figures due at 1330 GMT are expected to show 150,000 new non-farm jobs and an unchanged unemployment rate of 6.0 percent in November.  \par \par \uc2 But despite anticipation of a strong showing, many traders expected minimal movement if the data surpassed expectations.  \par \par \uc2 At 0530 GMT, the dollar traded around 108.40 yen , compared to 108.20 in late U.S. deals and a two-week low of 107.96 yen hit in New York on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The euro fetched $1.2080 , compared to around $1.2085 in late U.S. trade and off a record high of $1.2160 hit on Thursday. The euro was at 130.95 yen , compared to around 130.75 yen on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 MOF \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  STANCE UNCHANGED  \par \par \uc2 Some traders said market players were nesting on short-dollar positions in hopes that Japan's July-September gross domestic product would be revised upwards on Tuesday, noting that such an outcome could prompt a wave of dollar-selling.  \par \par \uc2 At the same time, Japanese importers moved to buy the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at current levels, suspecting the Japanese government was not happy to see the dollar below 108 yen.  \par \par \uc2 Japan has sold a record 17.8 trillion yen ($164.5 billion) this year in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . As a result, the country's external reserves hit a record $644.569 billion at the end of November, up $18.3 billion from October, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) said on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Following the announcement, Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, said there was no change in the government's stance of acting in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets as needed.  \par \par \uc2 "We will closely monitor markets and take measures as appropriate," he told reporters when asked about speculation that the government would have to slow spending to keep the yen down because it was nearing its limit on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds.  \par \par \uc2 Asked about any impact on the government's dwindling funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mizoguchi said: "I don't think it is necessary to comment on that. Our stance is unchanged."  \par \par \uc2 On Friday, the Nihon Keizai business daily reported that the government planned to raise the ceiling by 20 trillion yen to nearly 100 trillion yen when it compiles an extra budget for the current fiscal year, which ends in March.  \par \par \uc2 While such a move had long been anticipated in the market, a top MOF official told Reuters the ministry was considering a huge increase in the ceiling instead of an incremental rise - for instance boosting it to 150 trillion or 200 trillion yen, to ensure the cap never becomes an issue.  \par \par \uc2 "An important factor in the equation is to set the ceiling at such a level that it never becomes a factor in the minds of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market participants," the official said.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031205dzc5001s8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
