\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  says funds cap won't impede  \highlight22\uc2 fx intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Mari Terawaki  \par \uc2 757 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2003\par 05:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Dec 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sought on Friday to quash speculation it could scale back its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at curbing the yen's export-crimping rise just because of a legal cap on its yen borrowing for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Having conducted a record 17.8 trillion yen ($165 billion) of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first 11 months of the year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account managed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) is nearing its ceiling for yen-fund raising.  \par \par \uc2 But Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Zembei Mizoguchi said on Friday that Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy would not change, and a senior MOF official said there was still plenty of room to borrow under the existing cap.  \par \par \uc2 Another top MOF official told Reuters the ministry could significantly raise the ceiling - perhaps even doubling it - in the next fiscal year starting April to totally eradicate any possible speculation about a funding crunch.  \par \par \uc2 "There is no chance (\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) will hesitate to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market because \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds are declining," the first MOF official told reporters after the ministry released \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve figures for November.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's external reserves, long the world's biggest, grew further to record levels again in November after the ministry spent 1.6 trillion yen in a bid to contain the yen, which scaled three-year highs against the dollar during the month.  \par \par \uc2 Despite the continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar fell to 107.52 yen in late November, its lowest since November 2000 and down 10 percent in less than four months, raising concerns that Japan's export-driven economic recovery could stall.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was trading at around 108.20 yen on Friday, within striking distance of those lows.  \par \par \uc2 The reserves rose to $644.569 billion, up $18.3 billion from October, due mainly to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the euro's rise against the dollar, which boosted the dollar value of euro holdings.  \par \par \uc2 On the other side of the rise in external reserves is the MOF's bulging borrowing in yen.  \par \par \uc2 MORE OPTIONS  \par \par \uc2 Mizoguchi, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top financial diplomat, declined to comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds but added that the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy remained unchanged.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't think it is necessary to comment on that. Our stance is unchanged," he told reporters. "We will closely monitor markets and take measures as appropriate."  \par \par \uc2 The ministry raises yen funds for its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  account by issuing securities known in the money market as finance bills.  \par \par \uc2 The ceiling for the borrowing is currently 79 trillion yen and about six trillion yen is believed to be left under the cap.  \par \par \uc2 On Friday, the Nihon Keizai Shimbun business daily reported that the government planned to raise the ceiling by 20 trillion yen to near 100 trillion yen when it compiles an extra budget for the current fiscal year, which ends in March.  \par \par \uc2 While such a move had long been anticipated in the market, a top MOF official told Reuters the ministry was considering a huge increase in the ceiling instead of an incremental rise - for instance boosting it to 150 trillion or 200 trillion yen, to ensure the cap never becomes an issue.  \par \par \uc2 "An important factor in the equation is to set the ceiling at such a level that it never becomes a factor in the minds of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market participants," the official said.  \par \par \uc2 OTHER OPTIONS  \par \par \uc2 Mizoguchi said he could not comment on the newspaper report because a decision to compile an extra budget had not been made.  \par \par \uc2 Extra budgets have been a touchy issue for Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi, who has vowed to return the government to a balanced budget in a decade and has fought old-guard politicians demanding more public works spending to bolster the economy.  \par \par \uc2 But a small extra budget to cover an unforeseen increase in disaster relief funding and Japan's contribution to the reconstruction of Iraq is likely to be approved later this year.  \par \par \uc2 Ministry officials have said that if the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  account gets too close to the ceiling before the extra budget process is completed, the ministry can sell foreign securities - namely U.S. Treasury bills - from the account to the Bank of Japan in a repurchase pact and receive payment in yen.  \par \par \uc2 BOJ Policy Board member Hidehiko Haru said on Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had yet to receive such a request from the government but that it would consider terms of a deal if it did. ($1=108.23 yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031205dzc5001ek\par }\page 