\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  has enough funds for  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2 -MOF.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Mariko Hayashibara  \par \uc2 644 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2003\par 03:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Dec 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Ministry reiterated on Friday that it had enough funds available to continue to conduct \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , playing down speculation it may have to slow down its spending spree aimed at reining in the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Having spent 17.8 trillion yen ($165 billion) in the first 11 months of the year on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the ministry's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account is nearing its borrowing ceiling for yen, spurring speculation Japan could scale down its yen selling.  \par \par \uc2 Such speculation is one reason the yen has refused to back down from the three-year highs it set against the dollar last month, keeping authorities concerned that it could choke off Japan's export-driven economic recovery.  \par \par \uc2 "We still have enough (funds) at present," a senior ministry official told reporters after the ministry released \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve figures for November.  \par \par \uc2 "There is no chance (\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) will hesitate to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market because \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds are declining."  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's external reserves, long the world's biggest, grew further to record levels again in November after the ministry spent 1.6 trillion yen as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  scaled three-year highs.  \par \par \uc2 The reserves rose to $644.569 billion, up $18.3 billion from October, due mainly to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the euro's rise against the dollar, which boosted the dollar value of euro holdings.  \par \par \uc2 Despite the continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar fell to around 107.50 yen in late November, its lowest since November 2000 and down 10 percent in less than four months.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was trading at around 108.20 yen on Friday, within striking distance of those lows.  \par \par \uc2 MORE OPTIONS  \par \par \uc2 Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, declined to comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds but added that the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy remained unchanged.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't think it is necessary to comment on that. Our stance is unchanged," said Mizoguchi, the vice finance minister for international affairs.  \par \par \uc2 "We will closely monitor markets and take measures as appropriate," he told reporters as he arrived at his office.  \par \par \uc2 The ministry's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account - the war chest for the ministry's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - is believed to be within about six trillion yen of its borrowing ceiling for yen.  \par \par \uc2 Government sources have told Reuters the MOF is considering asking for a higher borrowing limit for the account, currently set at 79 trillion yen.  \par \par \uc2 On Friday, the Nihon Keizai Shimbun business daily reported that the government planned to raise the ceiling by 20 trillion yen to near 100 trillion yen when it compiles an extra budget for the current fiscal year, which ends in March.  \par \par \uc2 Mizoguchi said he could not comment on the report because a decision to compile an extra budget had not been made.  \par \par \uc2 Extra budgets have been a touchy issue for Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi, who has vowed to return the government to a balanced budget in a decade and has fought old-guard politicians demanding more public works spending to bolster the economy.  \par \par \uc2 But a small extra budget to cover an unforeseen increase in disaster relief funding and Japan's contribution to the reconstruction of Iraq is likely to be approved later this year.  \par \par \uc2 A revised \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account ceiling could be written into that budget document.  \par \par \uc2 Ministry officials have said that if the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account gets too close to the ceiling before the extra budget process is completed, the ministry can sell foreign securities - namely U.S. Treasury bills - from the account to the Bank of Japan in a repurchase pact and receive payment in yen.  \par \par \uc2 BOJ Policy Board member Hidehiko Haru said on Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had yet to receive such a request from the government but that it would consider terms of a deal if it did. ($1=108.23 yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031205dzc5000xd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
