\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar hits fresh record low against euro.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By John Parry  \par \uc2 626 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 2003\par 15:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, comments, changes byline, changes dateline, previous LONDON)  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Dec 4 (Reuters) - The dollar plumbed a record low against the euro for the fifth straight day on Thursday, after a weekly report on U.S. jobless claims hinted the labor market might be less robust than expected.  \par \par \uc2 Claims rose to 365,000 in the week to Nov. 29, overshooting economists' consensus forecasts for 350,000 new filings.  \par \par \uc2 Friday's U.S. employment report for November is now the dollar's main data focus, analysts said. A Reuters poll shows a median forecast for 150,000 jobs added to nonfarm payrolls.  \par \par \uc2 "I think that (the dollar's decline after the U.S. jobless claims report) is just underscoring the really bearish dollar tone in the environment. There is this asymmetric response that positive news isn't helping the dollar but negative news can push it lower," said Lauren Germain, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Banc of America Securities in New York.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't think the number itself was that bad, but just being higher than expectations was all that was needed," Germain added.  \par \par \uc2 Early on Thursday morning in New York, the euro was up 0.17 percent to $1.2135. Against the yen, the dollar was down 0.03 percent at 108.14 yen, near an area where traders become more wary of the possibility that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might undertake yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Against the Swiss franc the dollar was at 1.2829 francs, down 0.27 percent on the day.  \par \par \uc2 The pound was down 0.1 percent on the day at $1.7247.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier on Thursday, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held its minimum bid rate unchanged at 2 percent, as expected.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of England left its key official U.K. interest rate steady at 3.75 percent. A 25-basis-point rise in U.K. rates is widely expected early next year.  \par \par \uc2 HOW MUCH TOLERANCE FOR A STRONGER EURO?  \par \par \uc2 Worries that euro zone policymakers may not put up with a strong euro emerged in Asia after a report in the British Daily Telegraph, which the European Commission dismissed, that the EU was looking at controls to stop a surge in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Analysts were skeptical Brussels would impose the 1970s-style \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls suggested in the report but said the story prompted profit-taking on euro positions built up during the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent rally.  \par \par \uc2 "The latest move in the euro has really been a euro move because euro/yen is higher as well, which probably doesn't please European officials.... I don't think they are prepared to do anything about it. It does feel like a technical move," said Marcel Kasumovich, head of G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy with Merrill Lynch in New York.  \par \par \uc2 He cited barrier options at $1.2050 and near $1.22 for the euro. Barrier options give the holder a right to trade a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a set price for a specified time. But they become worthless if the market hits an agreed-upon price, so holders of such options sometimes buy or sell a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep their option from being triggered.  \par \par \uc2 The euro has risen by some 16 percent against the dollar this year and by as much as 2 percent in the past week.  \par \par \uc2 Most policymaker comments so far have indicated little concern with the euro's current levels.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar hit two-week lows against the yen around 107.98 due to persistent worries about the U.S. current account deficit and geopolitical tensions.  \par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar climbed to fresh six-year highs against the U.S. dollar around US$0.7381, according to Reuters data. (Additional reporting by Carolyn Cohn in London).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031204dzc4002wz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
