nd $0.8225 in October 2000.   \par \par \uc2 AUSSIE TAPS NEW HIGH   \par \par \uc2 The euro's rise was triggered in part by a leap in the Australian dollar in the wake of a rate hike by the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar rose to a six-year high of 73.32 U.S. cents after the Reserve Bank of Australia lifted the cash rate by a quarter point to 5.25 percent - by far the highest among industrialised countries - citing the strong domestic economy and improving global conditions.   \par \par \uc2 Although the move was widely expected, it boosted the Australian dollar's already solid attraction as a high-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The British pound, which also boasts relatively high interest rates, hit a new five-year high of $1.7320 before easing to around $1.7310, still above $1.7300 in late U.S. trade.   \par \par \uc2 The embattled dollar also hit two-week lows around 108.50 yen , although its fall was limited by the possibility of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold a record 17.8 trillion yen ($163.8 billion) so far this year to limit the harm the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise can inflict on exports and the overall economy.   \par \par \uc2 "Few people want to sell the dollar for the yen when there is strong wariness about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Masamichi Koike, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corp.   \par \par \uc2 Ono of Daiwa said: "The yen was bought in the past few months on hopes for a Japanese economic recovery. But with Japanese shares sort of leveling off these days, the yen may not rise as before."   \par \par \uc2 Still, many traders thought a retest of Monday's early peaks around 110 yen was also unlikely, given the greenback's repeated failure to rise much 